Ih99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Encountered Gerrit upload failure while pushing first priority bug asbestine-inaccurate-sanderling from worktree fix-async-stale-running at commit f9bd25f5abe15ddf68330efb32aac98d61c27a43. Exact error: remote unpack failed: error Missing tree 1af810df3393ce46cfd6c56338433a23c2555e09; remote rejected HEAD -> refs/for/main (n/a (unpacker error)). Will wait 10 minutes and retry once per known-issue protocol.","timestamp":1788830380010227001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator ruling recorded for this P1 interrupt: alarm/disk-pressure-adjacent recovery work is approved; mirror the environment's existing operational best practices; any alarms or prevention follow-ups must provide meaningful health signal, not noise. Taking incident response now before resuming alarm-wave work.","timestamp":1788832496646667001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Interim blast-radius update: receive-pack is not globally broken. From a fresh worktree at current origin/main (665d1d0480187) I created empty scratch commit fa547db55644 and normal upload `git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main` succeeded, creating Gerrit change 2813; I abandoned it immediately. Recent successful rebar changes were also created at 2026-09-08 01:24, 01:30, 01:32, and the scratch at 02:03 UTC. Current evidence points to pushes referencing specific missing server object(s)/history around older base 710a606b and trees 1959f268/1af810df, not all review uploads.","timestamp":1788833001347933001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Blast-radius follow-up: a second scratch upload from the exact older base named in the report (710a606b6d38) also succeeded normally and created Gerrit change 2814; I abandoned it immediately. Host quick checks show root 32%, /var/gerrit 24%, gate-scratch 29%, Docker build cache 5.8G reclaimable, and server-side git cat-file now resolves both reported missing trees 1959f268... and 1af810df... as tree objects. This makes the active outage non-reproducing at receive-pack as of 02:04 UTC; continuing with log/fsck correlation before any repair.","timestamp":1788833124705364001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Backup completed before any repository repair: EBS snapshot snap-058fc28c74eba365e of Gerrit data volume vol-06fa2e77a9dd97527 (/var/gerrit), started 2026-09-08T02:11:32Z, state completed. No Gerrit restart/downtime so far.","timestamp":1788833813009991001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA and recovery evidence. Observation: HTTP receive-pack rejected valid uploads with JGit FullConnectivityChecker MissingObjectException for tree 1959f268... at 2026-09-07T21:21/21:22Z and tree 1af810df... at 2026-09-08T01:19/01:24/01:26Z; earlier log entries show the same class for aa9f407e..., fb2069..., 4fe3561..., and 1440a442.... Hypothesis A (global receive-pack outage) was falsified: scratch normal pushes from current origin/main and from the reported older base 710a606b both succeeded, creating changes 2813 and 2814, then abandoned. Hypothesis B (persistent repository corruption/missing objects) was falsified by host and in-container checks: git cat-file resolves every logged tree, refs/heads/main and refs/changes/13/2813/1, /14/2814/1, /15/2815/1 resolve as commits, and git fsck --connectivity-only --no-dangling --no-reflogs is clean. Hypothesis C (transient missing object/visibility window during rapid submit/replication under disk pressure) best fits: the failed trees correspond to recently merged/uploaded objects; the objects are now present as loose objects with mtimes matching merge/push windows, receive-pack is healthy, and no bad packs/truncated loose objects were found by fsck. Disk evidence: at investigation time root was 32%, /var/gerrit 24%, gate-scratch 29%; BuildKit cache was 5.837GB and rebar-docker-buildkit-cache-high was ALARM from a prior 95% datapoint/missing-data window. Recovery: backed up /var/gerrit first with EBS snapshot snap-058fc28c74eba365e, fetched GitHub mirror main into the Gerrit repo to backfill any missing mirror-held objects, verified named trees and clean fsck, removed the temporary recovery ref, then pruned BuildKit cache to 0B (root 32% -> 25%). Verification: post-repair ordinary HEAD:refs/for/main push without --no-thin succeeded as change 2815 and was abandoned; main and refs/changes smoke refs remain readable; no Gerrit restart and no planned downtime. Prevention: feed this incident into the bounded disk-ceiling/root-disk family (scaup) and keep BuildKit/root pressure alarms meaningful rather than noisy; object-store repair should remain backup-first, fetch-from-mirror, fsck-verified, no aggressive GC until healthy.","timestamp":1788834096230005001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"While pushing rebased Gerrit change 2819 PS3 for complex-sassy-blackfly, Gerrit rejected the receive-pack with object-store unpacker failure: `remote unpack failed: error Missing blob ef992016d5f84faddb05a9a086341141a7aeebab`; remote rejected HEAD -> refs/for/main (n/a (unpacker error)). This is the same live object-store class; I have not touched Gerrit git data or restarted Gerrit. Per blackfly instructions I am doing one bounded 10-minute wait before a single retry.","timestamp":1788846244414445001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788816289632378477,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6fee6b0a-e20a-467a-98fe-9180b5a63d80","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"47be-ce45-484a-4cc2"}],"description":"## Problem\nGerrit rejects a valid review upload from a clean worktree with `remote unpack failed: error Missing tree 1959f268184dce88f62132173dfbf24e823ceb89`. The failure blocks comment-remediation changes from entering review and appears to be Gerrit repository/object-store health, not the patch.\n\n## Evidence\n- Worktree: `/Users/joeoakhart/comment-remediation-47be`.\n- Commit: `be29a0057028f539a34f79658fb57f09d40f0422`; parent and current `origin/main`: `710a606b6d38bafc0f2c6684711b08811d26529e`.\n- Normal upload `git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main` was rejected before a change was created.\n- A second upload with `git push --no-thin gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main` failed with the identical missing-tree object.\n- Locally, `git cat-file -t 1959f268184dce88f62132173dfbf24e823ceb89` returns `tree`, and the leaf revision walk reports no missing objects.\n- No server-side repair or further retry was attempted in the comment/documentation session.\n\n## Investigation plan\n- Reproduce against the Gerrit repository and inspect the receive-pack/JGit logs for the rejected upload.\n- Verify Gerrit's `main` ref, reachable object graph, alternates/promisor configuration, recent replication, and repository consistency around the named tree.\n- Determine why a non-thin pack still leaves the server resolving the tree as missing.\n- Repair the server repository through the supported backup/recovery path, then verify ordinary review upload and receive-pack health.\n- Document the root cause, blast radius, safe recovery, and recurrence prevention.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The missing-tree rejection is reproduced or conclusively tied to retained server logs.\n- [x] The precise Gerrit repository/object-store root cause is proven with concrete evidence.\n- [x] Repository integrity is restored through a backed-up, supported recovery procedure.\n- [x] A normal `HEAD:refs/for/main` review upload succeeds without `--no-thin`.\n- [x] Existing refs/changes and `main` remain valid and no review data is lost.\n- [x] Recovery and prevention evidence are recorded on this ticket.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"c2e69544-4449-45ab-9f67-e25eb8edf1ac","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["gerrit","infrastructure","git","blocking"],"ticket_id":"7744-3e35-b2c4-40c2","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Gerrit rejects review uploads with a missing tree","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f40a07fd-1479-4c17-909d-c076ab54c06f","58e4959a-f9cb-4bf0-a0dd-622529b85f80","eb5a2c3e-3016-47d3-8813-42d51cf40a47","1050cb3b-a3a8-4c26-8387-32b981790f59","67bc0f87-d1c3-47cf-8b5d-fb2028288fd4","25a154f5-90ab-4838-8803-ea29720d77f7","2b08312f-fe92-4afc-8a2b-40a4524f59c5","0bab5d0b-3d19-4e6b-9268-8e51b769f46d","ac13a4d7-45e8-47f3-87c6-febda60cc703","befd4206-0166-40f8-9cf9-45abdaaf0e73","c2e69544-4449-45ab-9f67-e25eb8edf1ac","2449d8f2-6f61-4326-b9dd-8c971ea4649b","88e23994-035c-44ac-85b4-db060ed2fc9f"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788846244414445002,"uuid":"a8567119-10a5-44c2-b6d8-da6e2af68412"}